+  <header class="shell topbar">
+    <a class="wordmark" href="#top" aria-label="Team home"><span class="mark">{ }</span> A very real team site</a>
+    <button class="theme-toggle" id="themeToggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false">☾ Night mode</button>
+  </header>
+
+  <main id="top" class="shell">
+    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="team-title">
+      <p class="eyebrow">Paderborn University · M.Sc. Computer Science</p>
+      <h1 id="team-title">The Prompt Engineers <span>Who Can't Center a Div</span></h1>
+      <p class="hero-copy">Five computer scientists, a suspicious amount of chai, and a group project that is—in a refreshing change of pace—actually about the group.</p>
+      <div class="hero-meta" aria-label="Team facts">
+        <span class="pill hot">5 humans</span><span class="pill">1 shared future</span><span class="pill">0 divs centered (allegedly)</span>
+      </div>
+    </section>
+
+    <div class="section-head">
+      <h2>Meet the humans<br>behind the prompts.</h2>
+      <p>Each comes with a specialty, a strong opinion, and at least one reason an AI still needs supervision.</p>
+    </div>
+
+    <section class="team-grid" aria-label="Team members">
+      <article class="card">
+        <div class="card-top"><img class="portrait" src="{{image:nirav.jpg}}" alt="Photo of Nirav"><div><span class="member-number">01 / THE SYSTEMS PERSON</span><h3>Nirav</h3><p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, 1st semester at Paderborn University; B.Tech. in Computer Engineering.</p></div></div>
+        <div class="card-body"><p class="interests"><strong>Into:</strong> Backend systems, table tennis, and trying every street food stall at a new place.</p>
+          <div class="detail"><span class="detail-label">Fun fact</span><p>I have named every one of my laptops after a Bollywood villain.</p></div>
+          <div class="detail"><span class="detail-label">AI, today</span><p>AI is a fast junior developer that never gets tired but also never says "I'm not sure". It saves me hours on boilerplate, but I still read every line before it goes anywhere near main.</p></div>
